{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nBest-effort tickets-branch push failures that are EXPECTED and AUTO-HANDLED are surfaced to\nagent-visible stderr at WARNING with wording that primes LLM agent sessions to assume the store\nis broken and burn tokens investigating. Two 2026-08-21 session reports (~12 concurrent\nwriters) show agents halting work to inspect `push.py` for a state that heals on the next\nsuccessful write. Operator ruling (2026-08-21): \"If these issues are expected and handled\nautomatically, we need to stop surfacing them to sessions because it primes them to assume\nthere's an issue and burn tokens investigating.\" Ruling update (2026-08-21): \"We should\nsuppress the message under normal load. This is noise, not an outage signal.\" — so under\nnormal load (ordinary contention losses, transient transport retries, the routine\nunpushed-backlog suffix) the messages are suppressed from agent-visible output entirely\n(DEBUG at most), and a merely non-zero or shared backlog count is NOT an outage signal.\n\n## Offending messages (all logger.warning, agent-visible)\n\n1. `push.py:342` — \"tickets branch push failed after 3 retries: <raw git stderr><suffix>\" after\n   losing a CONTENTION race; raw git stderr pattern-matches corruption to an LLM (`unable to\n   update local ref`, `! [rejected]`). The sibling terminal site `push.py:323` \"terminal push\n   failed after recovery\" is the same lost-contention outcome and gets the same treatment.\n2. `push_classify.py:225` — \"tickets branch push hit a transient transport fault (attempt x/y),\n   retrying\" — the code is already retrying itself; WARNING is pure worry-bait (INFO material).\n3. `push_state.py:148` `unpushed_summary` — the \"(N unpushed commits on origin/tickets..HEAD)\"\n   suffix: \"HEAD\" is the TRACKER's HEAD but a session reads it as its code worktree HEAD; the\n   count escalates across ALL concurrent sessions; nothing states the self-healing contract.\n\n## What must STAY loud (bug 2a76's rationale is still valid)\n\n- Policy declines (hook declined, GH013, branch protection) — permanent, operator-actionable.\n- Strict-mode callers — PushDeliveryError already raises; unchanged.\n- A PERSISTENT/growing backlog — fsck PUSH_PENDING and the durable rebar-push-pending marker\n  are the operator channels; a terminal failure with a GROWING count may stay WARNING.\n\n## Approach\n\nLogging/wording only — no change to push behavior, classification, retries, or the durable\nmarker. Encode expected-and-self-healing vs operator-actionable at the existing reporting seam\n(`push_classify`, the \"how is a failure reported\" module):\n\n1. Reword `push_state.unpushed_summary` to name the tickets branch explicitly (no bare\n   `..HEAD`) and state the self-healing contract in the text: the commits are committed\n   locally and publish on the next successful push. The suffix is shared by every backlog\n   message (including the strict `PushDeliveryError` text), so it stays factual for policy\n   declines too — the \"expected under concurrent writers; no action needed\" clause is\n   appended only on the demoted expected path (point 3).\n2. Add `push_state.backlog_grew(tracker, remote_ref)` — a read-only helper comparing the\n   current `unpushed_count` against the `unpushed` count already recorded in the previous\n   push-pending marker (state the marker already stores; no new persistent state). Ambiguity\n   (no prior marker, non-numeric counts) resolves to False — growth must be PROVEN before a\n   report escalates to operator-loud.\n3. Add a `push_classify` helper returning (log level, backlog suffix) for a terminal\n   best-effort push failure: WARNING for a policy decline in the terminal stderr or a\n   proven-growing backlog; otherwise DEBUG with the appended \"expected under concurrent\n   tickets writers — no action needed\" clause. Called BEFORE `_raise_if_strict` records the\n   new marker (which overwrites the previous count the growth check reads).\n4. Switch the two terminal lost-contention sites in `push.py` (retry-exhausted ~342 and\n   terminal-after-recovery ~323) from `logger.warning` to `logger.log(level, ...)` using that\n   helper. The pinned literals \"failed after %s retries\" and \"terminal push failed after\n   recovery\" are appended-to, never reworded — the epoch-guard negative assertions\n   (test_epoch_guard_matrix / test_epoch_guard_reconciliation) are honored, not retargeted.\n5. Demote every mid-retry transient-transport notice from WARNING to DEBUG, wording stating\n   the retry is automatic and needs no action: `_retry_transport_or_stop` in `push_classify`\n   plus the same-class recovery-leg notices in `push_recovery.py` (merge-leg ~:293, fetch-leg\n   ~:378). The TERMINAL transport/policy warnings stay WARNING (bug 2a76 / f61c rationale).\n\nTests pinning the old wording/level are consciously retargeted in the same change:\n`test_push_strict.py` (mid-retry capture level), `test_push_strict_happy.py` and\n`test_push_rejection_surfacing.py` (the \"unpushed commits on origin/tickets..HEAD\" suffix).\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/_store/push_state.py — `unpushed_summary` rewording; new `backlog_grew` helper.\n- src/rebar/_store/push_classify.py — mid-retry demotion to INFO; new terminal-severity helper.\n- src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py — demote the merge-leg and fetch-leg mid-retry\n  transient-transport notices to INFO (same class, same wording contract).\n- src/rebar/_store/push.py — the two terminal contention log sites call the helper and log at\n  its level (message literals appended-to only).\n- tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py — retarget: expected-case silence at INFO\n  and above + worry-free wording + growing-backlog escalation + no bare `..HEAD`.\n- tests/unit/test_push_strict.py, tests/unit/test_push_strict_happy.py,\n  tests/unit/test_push_rejection_surfacing.py — retarget the pinned wording/level assertions.\n\n## Testing\n\nRED→GREEN (the retargeted tests fail on current main, pass after the fix), all caplog-level\nassertions on the `rebar._store` loggers:\n\n- Expected case: a retry-exhausted lost contention race (every push non-fast-forward-rejected,\n  recovery merges clean, no prior marker) emits NO record at INFO or above; a DEBUG record\n  carries \"failed after N retries\", names the tickets branch, and states \"expected under\n  concurrent\" + \"no action needed\"; no message contains bare `..HEAD`.\n- Mid-retry transient transport notice is captured at DEBUG, below INFO.\n- Growing backlog: with a prior marker recording a smaller `unpushed` count, the same terminal\n  contention failure logs at WARNING (the sanctioned escalation).\n- Preserved loud cases: the existing real-git policy-decline suite\n  (test_push_rejection_surfacing) still passes at WARNING with reason + backlog count; strict\n  callers still raise PushDeliveryError (test_push_strict / test_push_strict_happy).\n\nVerification commands: targeted pytest on the push/epoch-guard suites\n(tests/unit/test_push_*.py, tests/unit/test_epoch_guard_matrix.py,\ntests/integration/test_epoch_guard_reconciliation.py, tests/unit/test_commit_and_push*,\ntests/interfaces/store/test_fsck_push_pending.py), then `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A lost contention race on a best-effort write emits NOTHING at INFO or above (DEBUG at\n      most), while the state remains observable via push_status()/fsck PUSH_PENDING/marker.\n      Checked by the new caplog test (no records >= INFO) plus the marker/fsck suites green.\n- [ ] Mid-retry transient transport messages (push_classify + both push_recovery legs) are\n      DEBUG or below. Checked by caplog level assertions in test_push_strict.py and the new\n      suite.\n- [ ] Every remaining backlog message names the tickets branch explicitly (no bare `..HEAD`),\n      with the self-healing contract stated in the message text. Checked by wording assertions\n      on the emitted records and the retargeted strict-message pins.\n- [ ] Policy declines, strict failures, and a proven-GROWING backlog remain WARNING/raise,\n      byte-compatible where tests pin them (reason token, GH013 passthrough, backlog count).\n      Checked by test_push_rejection_surfacing and test_push_strict staying green.\n- [ ] Tests pin expected-case silence at INFO and above, worry-free wording, plus the\n      preserved loud cases. Checked by the retargeted test module failing RED on current main\n      and passing GREEN."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787341815181298001,"uuid":"d6395f1f-8380-4b4b-b4b5-977327c3ef66"}